# Transcribed from Table II of the paper below (one monomer of each of the four chains A-D; the
# second monomer of each chain comes from the 2-fold screw axis along b, space group P21 as stated
# in the paper). Bars over numbers in the scan (negative values) checked on the page image.
# This is the paper's simplified 1955 model (all chain angles 112 deg, idealised amide), so some
# bond lengths are rough (C=O 1.15 A in chain A, amide C-C 1.19 A in chains B and D): peak
# positions are reliable, relative intensities only approximate.
# Hydrogen atoms and displacement parameters are not listed in the paper. Not a COD entry.
# Molecule B, carbonyl O: z printed as -0.027 (molecules A, C, D use -0.007, 0.473, 0.473); kept as printed.
